[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65815,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Kaposi sarcoma (KS) is a locally aggressive endothelial proliferation that usually presents with cutaneous lesions in the form of multiple patches, plaques, or nodules, but it may also involve mucosal sites, lymph nodes, and visceral organs. KS is uniformly associated with human herpesvirus (HHV8) infection, and it is an example of a virus-induced vascular proliferation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65816,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9140/3 Kaposi sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65817,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B57.Z &amp; XH36A5 Kaposi sarcoma of unspecified primary site &amp; Kaposi sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65818,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65819,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65820,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>KS can be limited to the vulva or disseminated {16363765}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65821,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vulvar KS manifests as bluish-red single or multiple masses {7675418} or exophytic indurated nodules, or it can mimic a papilloma or abscess {15898528}. Lesions can be asymptomatic or associated with pain or pruritus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65822,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions typically occur in the second to fourth decade of life, or rarely postmenopausally {492632; 26082598}. AIDS-associated KS {16105346; 15881707; 11054682; 15898528} and classic KS {26082598} are frequent types.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65823,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Infection with HHV8 (KS-associated herpesvirus) is required, although not sufficient for disease induction.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65824,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Disease expression results from complex interactions among genetic, immunological, and environmental factors {11423257; 11536246}. HHV8 (also called KS-associated herpesvirus), which is a mainly sexually transmitted DNA virus, can be detected in all forms of KS (&gt;&nbsp;95% of AIDS-related and non-related cases) {7723505; 12244338; 10749966}, with genetic variants linked to specific populations {20079510}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65825,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>KS presents as variably sized haemorrhagic nodules or necrotic masses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65826,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the patch stage of KS, numerous small slit-like vascular spaces lined by flat to oval endothelial cells dissect surrounding collagen fibres. Ovoid and spindle endothelial cells with minimal or no atypia are admixed with lymphoplasmacytic infiltrates, extravasated erythrocytes, and haemosiderin deposits, sometimes with intracellular/extracellular hyaline globules. In the plaque and nodular stages, all features are exaggerated. Lesions express endothelial markers (e.g. CD31, CD34, ERG) and lymphatic markers (e.g. D2-40), with almost invariable nuclear HHV8 positivity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65827,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65828,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65829,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> slit-like vascular spaces, dissection of collagen fibres, extravasated erythrocytes, and/or haemosiderin deposition.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> HHV8 immunohistochemistry (in selected cases).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65830,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65831,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 429,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Disease evolution depends on the KS type and extent. Rare metastatic cases have been reported {15898528}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:25:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]